2026-09-25T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2256) 'What is not settled
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2256) '- **Throughput.** Bulk game traffic needs the binary-translated
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2256) '  guest to keep up with a native QUIC stack. Nothing is measured
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2256) '  yet; the comparison is the same stack built native against the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2256) '  translated guest, same payload, same link.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2256) '- **Per-call instruction budget.** Translation shortens a TLS 1.3
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2256) '  handshake but does not remove the sandbox's per-call limit, so
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2256) '  the budget for this guest is set from a measured handshake.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2256) '- **Transport.** WebTransport is the proposal; ENet through the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2256) '  existing ENet sandbox is the fallback if the translated QUIC
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2256) '  guest cannot carry the traffic.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2256) '- **Licences.** picoquic, picotls and mbedTLS are MIT or
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2256) '  Apache-2.0. libriscv and godot-sandbox are BSD-3-Clause, so
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2256) '  an MIT-or-Apache-only rule needs an exception for the host.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2256) '- **Which peer.** A zone server the operator runs, on owned
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2256) '  hardware or the existing hosting; the choice decides who can
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2256) '  read that peer's memory.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2256) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

